<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 39 pct sold, yield 3.57 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 1-wk T-bills 39 pct sold, yield 3.57 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 10 billion levs of one-week discount T-bills was 39.45 percent sold on Wednesday, yielding 3.57 percent to maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said on Thursday. @</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3010997008</p>
<p> Auction date		     January 15, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date			 January 16, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		    January 23, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    7,018.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		96.31 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    3,944.9 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     96.55 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    3.57 pct @</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
